{"study_accession":"PRJNA556960","secondary_study_accession":"SRP216571","title":"RNA-sequencing of human peripheral blood mononuclear cells from Tanzanian children","description":"Total RNA sequencing of peripheral blood mononuclear cells (PBMC) from Tanzanian children from the Phase 3 trial of the RTS,S (Mosquirix) vaccine (ClinicalTrials.gov NCT00866619). At baseline (B0) children were between 5-17 months of age at baseline (B0), and were 32 months older at B32. Overall design: The RNA-sequencing data compliments a much larger immune-phenotyping study. Where there was sufficient cells remaining after flow-cytometry experiments, cells were stored in RNA-later. Samples from time-points B0 (n=21) and B32 (n=9) were then sequenced to determine how the blood transcriptome changes over time. Three participants had samples were sequenced at both B0 and B32. ","pubmed":"32024802","geo_series":"","n_samples":30,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN12385253","study_accession":"PRJNA556960","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"2895_M0","description":"2895_M0","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM3983138","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2020-02-21","attributes":[["source_name","Blood"],["timepoint","B0"],["cell_type","peripheral blood mononuclear cells"],["tissue","Blood"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR9849517","experiment_accession":"SRX6604129","library_layout":"SINGLE","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina HiSeq 2500","read_count":79771307,"base_count":3988565350,"first_public":"2020-02-21","experiment_title":"Illumina HiSeq 2500 sequencing: GSM3983138: 2895_M0 Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"labels":[],"single_cell":false},{"sample_accession":"SAMN12385254","study_accession":"PRJNA556960","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"2893_M32","description":"2893_M32","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM3983137","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2020-02-21","attributes":[["source_name","Blood"],["timepoint","B32"],["cel